The SquashFS images in this folder were made by the repository's
tools/squashfs-images/make.py, with squashfs-tools 4.6.1's mksquashfs as
scripts/testdata.py builds it (the mksquashfs set), from a small tree of
files the script writes: three files, one of 9,000 bytes (two 4 KiB blocks
and a tail), a second name for one of them, a directory, a symbolic link,
and from mksquashfs's pseudo file a block device, a FIFO and extended
attributes:

  python3 scripts/testdata.py fetch --set mksquashfs
  python3 tools/squashfs-images/make.py small \
      "${HIVEPACK_TESTDATA:-target/testdata}/mksquashfs/mksquashfs" testdata/squashfs

There is one image for each compressor (gzip, lzma, lzo, xz, lz4, zstd), and
uncompressed.sqfs, gzip with nothing compressed (-noI -noD -noF -noX).
manifest.txt lists the arguments each was made with. They are under the
repository's license:

